ALL ABOUT MYSELF

My name is Bernice Kwao. I am 24 years old, and I was born on 25th March 2002. I come from Odumase Krobo in the Eastern Region of Ghana. I completed my Senior High School education in 2019.

I am a hardworking, ambitious, caring and determined young woman. I consider myself a little shy, but I am friendly, respectful and always willing to learn new things. I believe in treating people with kindness and respect.

I currently serve in the Ghana Armed Forces as a Lance Corporal. Being in the military has taught me discipline, teamwork, patience, loyalty and responsibility. I take pride in my work and hope to continue growing in my career.

In my free time, I enjoy listening to music, watching movies, spending time with friends and family, and learning new things. My favourite food is Banku with okra soup.

I also have an interest in personal development, technology and education. I enjoy discovering new ideas and improving my knowledge and skills.

My future ambitions are to advance in my military career, further my education, become financially independent and achieve my personal goals. I also hope to become a successful, responsible and independent woman who can make a positive difference in society.

In conclusion, I believe that life is a continuous learning process. I know that success requires patience, determination and hard work. I am committed to working towards my dreams and becoming a better version of myself every day.
